text The background music switches to a mysterious-sounding track.
text As the curtain tucks us away from the outside world, the atmosphere actually feels rather legitimate.
text Fortune tellers in their shop probably give off this same atmosphere too.
text Fujibayashi looks at me; her eyes look as if she's struck with wonder.
text No, rather, she is struck with wonder.
text As proof, the stiffness that I felt in her hand has completely disappeared.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hm?
text Suddenly, a change occurs in the world inside the monitor.
text The planets, which had been revolving around the sun, now start to separate to opposite ends of the screen.
text They then blink several times, and start to fade away.
text At almost exactly the same time, the crystal ball which we laid our hands on starts to glow faintly.
text Before long, all the planets have completely disappeared, and the sun draws near us.
text The sun accelerates toward us, expanding to cover the monitor, and turns the screen white.
